WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.824 --> 00:00:04.126
IN THIS HORRIFIC MASSACRE.

00:00:02.758 --> 00:00:04.627
&gt;&gt; Tucker: RICK, THANK YOU FOR

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.695
THAT.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.029
I APPRECIATE YOUR PERSPECTIVE ON

00:00:06.829 --> 00:00:09.732
THAT.

00:00:07.163 --> 00:00:11.667
&gt;&gt; ALWAYS A PLEASURE, TUCKER.

00:00:09.866 --> 00:00:13.603
&gt;&gt; Tucker: A STUDENT AT

00:00:11.801 --> 00:00:15.071
MARJORY STONEMAN DOUGLAS WHERE

00:00:13.736 --> 00:00:17.774
THE SHOOTING OCCURRED, TRAPPED

00:00:15.204 --> 00:00:18.674
IN A CLASSROOM WHEN THE S.W.A.T.

00:00:17.907 --> 00:00:20.610
TEAM STRUGGLED LOOK AND

00:00:18.808 --> 00:00:22.578
STRUGGLED TO GET HER OUT.

00:00:20.743 --> 00:00:23.780
THANK YOU FOR COMING ON.

00:00:22.712 --> 00:00:26.416
WHAT DID YOU EXPERIENCE TODAY?

00:00:23.913 --> 00:00:28.418
&gt;&gt; THE LAST 20 MINUTES OF CLASS

00:00:26.549 --> 00:00:29.919
THERE WAS A FIRE DRILL, BUT IT'S

00:00:28.551 --> 00:00:33.022
REALLY WEIRD RIGHT AWAY, BECAUSE

00:00:30.053 --> 00:00:35.024
WE JUST HAD ONE THIS MORNING, SO

00:00:33.156 --> 00:00:37.093
EVERYONE ALREADY KNEW THAT

00:00:35.158 --> 00:00:39.362
SOMEBODY HAD EITHER PULLED IT OR

00:00:37.226 --> 00:00:43.800
IT WAS SET OFF, AND IT COULD NOT

00:00:39.495 --> 00:00:45.802
HAVE BEEN RINGING FOR MORE THAN

00:00:43.933 --> 00:00:47.270
5 MINUTES, MORE THAN 2 MINUTES,

00:00:45.935 --> 00:00:49.005
BECAUSE THAT BY THE TIME I HAD

00:00:47.403 --> 00:00:49.973
REACHED THE STAIRWELL IT HAD

00:00:49.138 --> 00:00:52.675
ALREADY STOPPED, AND EVERYBODY

00:00:50.106 --> 00:00:55.078
STOOD THERE NOT KNOWING EXACTLY

00:00:52.809 --> 00:00:58.314
WHAT TO DO AND WE JUST KIND OF

00:00:55.211 --> 00:01:00.049
LOOKED AROUND UNTIL WE HEARD

00:00:58.448 --> 00:01:01.417
THREE OR FOUR LOUD BANGS AND

00:01:00.183 --> 00:01:05.588
EVERYONE WHO WAS GOING DOWN THE

00:01:01.551 --> 00:01:08.157
STAIRS AND RAN BACK UP, AND

00:01:05.722 --> 00:01:09.959
ABOUT I WANT TO SAY OVER 100

00:01:08.291 --> 00:01:17.801
STUDENTS JUST TRYING TO RUN INTO

00:01:10.093 --> 00:01:18.468
A CLASSROOM AND SHUT THE DOOR.

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:19.169
THERE WERE KIDS IN MY CLASS

00:01:18.602 --> 00:01:19.903
RUNNING THROUGH THE CORNER AND

00:01:19.302 --> 00:01:22.539
JUMPING OVER DESKS AND TRYING TO

00:01:20.037 --> 00:01:24.975
GET BEHIND THE TEACHER'S DESK

00:01:22.673 --> 00:01:27.177
AND IT WAS A MESS OF --

00:01:25.108 --> 00:01:27.611
&gt;&gt; Tucker: WAS THE TEACHER IN

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:29.680
THE ROOM?

00:01:27.744 --> 00:01:30.180
&gt;&gt; MY TEACHER WAS NOT THERE

00:01:30.013 --> 00:01:31.281
TODAY.

00:01:30.313 --> 00:01:39.156
WE HAD A SUB, AND YOU COULD TELL

00:01:31.415 --> 00:01:41.224
THAT HE DID NOT KNOW WHAT TO DO.

00:01:39.289 --> 00:01:42.225
AT FIRST SHE THOUGHT IT WAS SOME

00:01:41.358 --> 00:01:44.795
KIND OF MESSED UP DRILL.

00:01:42.359 --> 00:01:47.030
BUT THEN WE STARTED TO SMELL

00:01:44.928 --> 00:01:48.632
STUFF LIKE SMOKE AND GUNPOWDER,

00:01:47.497 --> 00:01:50.233
AND OUR PARENTS WERE CALLING US

00:01:48.765 --> 00:01:51.234
AND FREAKING OUT AND CALLING

00:01:51.368 --> 00:01:57.207
BUT THEN OTHER KIDS WERE

00:01:55.672 --> 00:01:59.810
SHUSHING THEM TO BE QUIET.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:01.178
IT SEEMED LIKE WE WERE THERE FOR

00:01:59.943 --> 00:02:03.046
HOURS, BUT JUST NOT KNOWING

00:02:01.311 --> 00:02:06.016
ANYTHING OR WHAT WAS GOING ON.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:07.617
ONLY HEARING THE SIRENS OUTSIDE.

00:02:06.149 --> 00:02:07.918
&gt;&gt; Tucker: DID YOU LOCK THE

00:02:07.751 --> 00:02:12.189
DOOR?

00:02:08.051 --> 00:02:14.191
&gt;&gt; THE DOOR WAS ALREADY LOCKED.

00:02:12.322 --> 00:02:15.225
&gt;&gt; Tucker: DID YOU HAVE YOUR

00:02:14.324 --> 00:02:15.992
PHONE WITH YOU?

00:02:15.792 --> 00:02:17.527
&gt;&gt; YES.

00:02:16.126 --> 00:02:20.030
MY VERY FIRST INSTINCT WAS TO

00:02:17.661 --> 00:02:21.865
TAKE A VIDEO OF THE SOUND AND

00:02:20.163 --> 00:02:24.601
SEND IT TO MY PARENTS AND TELL

00:02:21.998 --> 00:02:25.969
THEM THAT I AM OKAY IN THE

00:02:24.735 --> 00:02:27.237
CLASSROOM.

00:02:26.103 --> 00:02:29.606
&gt;&gt; Tucker: DID THEY RESPOND?

00:02:27.371 --> 00:02:33.010
&gt;&gt; YES, ALMOST IMMEDIATELY.

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:34.978
&gt;&gt; Tucker: WHAT DID THEY SAY?

00:02:33.143 --> 00:02:36.814
&gt;&gt; BOTH OF THEM WERE JUST VERY

00:02:35.112 --> 00:02:37.915
CONFUSED AND ASKING ME IF I WAS

00:02:36.947 --> 00:02:41.118
OKAY AND WHERE I WAS AND WHAT

00:02:38.048 --> 00:02:46.890
BUILDING I WAS IN.

00:02:41.251 --> 00:02:48.092
AND IF I KNEW WHAT WAS GOING ON.

00:02:47.024 --> 00:02:51.428
JUST KEEP TALKING TO THEM NO

00:02:48.225 --> 00:02:52.997
MATTER WHAT.

00:02:51.562 --> 00:02:54.431
&gt;&gt; Tucker: SO YOU TEXT THEM

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:55.499
WHILE THE SHOOTING IS GOING ON,

00:02:54.565 --> 00:02:58.102
THEY TEXTED YOU BACK.

00:02:55.633 --> 00:02:58.602
THEY MUST HAVE JUST BEEN

00:02:58.235 --> 00:02:59.970
PANICKED.

00:02:58.736 --> 00:03:03.307
WHAT WAS YOUR REUNION LIKE WITH

00:03:00.104 --> 00:03:09.480
YOUR PARENTS?

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:11.215
&gt;&gt; UM, AS SOON AS I LEFT THE

00:03:09.613 --> 00:03:11.916
SCHOOL I WAS CROSSING THE STREET

00:03:11.348 --> 00:03:12.383
AND THEY KEPT HAVING US TURN

00:03:12.049 --> 00:03:13.484
AROUND.

00:03:12.516 --> 00:03:17.221
I WAS ON THE PHONE WITH MY MOM

00:03:13.617 --> 00:03:18.589
TRYING TO FIGURE OUT WHERE SHE

00:03:17.355 --> 00:03:22.026
WAS, BUT SHE SAID SHE WAS GOING

00:03:18.723 --> 00:03:24.195
TOWARDS THE END, AND AS SOON AS

00:03:22.159 --> 00:03:25.429
I SAW HER EYE JUST RAN TO HER,

00:03:24.328 --> 00:03:26.464
AND MY DAD RAN.

00:03:25.563 --> 00:03:27.298
MY LITTLE SISTER WAS THERE AND

00:03:26.597 --> 00:03:29.500
WE WERE JUST CRYING AND HUGGING

00:03:27.431 --> 00:03:31.969
EACH OTHER.

00:03:29.633 --> 00:03:33.171
&gt;&gt; Tucker: THAT IS AN

00:03:32.103 --> 00:03:34.205
EMOTIONAL -- JUST EMOTIONAL

00:03:33.304 --> 00:03:35.506
THINKING ABOUT THAT.

00:03:34.338 --> 00:03:37.041
YOU WERE LED OUT OF THE

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:37.875
CLASSROOM AND THE SCHOOL BY A

00:03:37.175 --> 00:03:41.078
S.W.A.T. TEAM, WHAT DID YOU SEE

00:03:38.009 --> 00:03:46.417
ON YOUR WAY OUT?

00:03:41.212 --> 00:03:47.351
&gt;&gt; I TRIED NOT TO LOOK, BUT

00:03:46.551 --> 00:03:49.720
THERE WAS BLOOD AND GUNPOWDER

00:03:47.485 --> 00:03:51.422
AND BODIES JUST ALL OVER THE

00:03:49.854 --> 00:03:53.891
PLACE.

00:03:51.556 --> 00:03:56.260
WE WERE STEPPING OVER PUDDLES OF

00:03:54.025 --> 00:03:59.931
BLOOD AND JUST TRYING NOT TO

00:03:56.394 --> 00:04:04.802
LOOK.

00:04:00.064 --> 00:04:05.503
&gt;&gt; Tucker: SO ALL OF THE

00:04:04.936 --> 00:04:06.804
STUDENTS IN THE CLASS THAT YOU

00:04:05.636 --> 00:04:07.572
WERE AND GOT OUT SAFELY, IS THAT

00:04:06.938 --> 00:04:09.774
CORRECT?

00:04:07.705 --> 00:04:11.976
&gt;&gt; I AM PRETTY SURE, YES.

00:04:09.907 --> 00:04:12.877
ALL OF THE STUDENTS THAT WERE IN

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:14.612
THE CLASS WITH ME WHEN THE DOOR

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:16.814
WAS SHUT ARE SAFE.

00:04:14.745 --> 00:04:17.448
&gt;&gt; Tucker: HAD YOU HEARD OF

00:04:17.115 --> 00:04:20.018
THE SHOOTER?

00:04:17.582 --> 00:04:20.418
NIKOLAS CRUZ, HAD YOU HEARD THAT

00:04:20.151 --> 00:04:22.320
NAME BEFORE?

00:04:20.551 --> 00:04:24.389
&gt;&gt; NO, I HAD NEVER HEARD HIS

00:04:22.453 --> 00:04:24.989
NAME OR MET HIM OR ANYTHING LIKE

00:04:24.522 --> 00:04:28.193
THAT.

00:04:25.123 --> 00:04:29.594
HE IS A COMPLETE STRANGER TO ME.

00:04:28.326 --> 00:04:32.096
&gt;&gt; Tucker: HE WAS EXPELLED

00:04:29.727 --> 00:04:32.564
FROM YOUR SCHOOL, YOU DON'T KNOW

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:34.299
WHY?

00:04:32.697 --> 00:04:38.737
&gt;&gt; NO.

00:04:34.432 --> 00:04:41.172
&gt;&gt; Tucker: INTERESTING.

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:42.040
FINALLY, HEYLEE, HAVE YOU TALKED

00:04:41.306 --> 00:04:45.210
TO YOUR CLASSMATES SINCE YOU

00:04:42.173 --> 00:04:46.611
LEFT THE SCHOOL, HOW ARE YOU

00:04:45.343 --> 00:04:47.445
DOING?

00:04:46.745 --> 00:04:49.814
&gt;&gt; ONE OF MY BEST FRIENDS WAS

00:04:47.579 --> 00:04:50.548
WITH ME IN THE ENTIRE TIME FROM

00:04:49.948 --> 00:04:52.350
THE STAIRCASE TO THE CLASSROOM

00:04:50.682 --> 00:04:54.219
TO LEAVING THE SCHOOL, AND WE

00:04:52.484 --> 00:04:56.988
HAVE BEEN CHECKING UP ON EACH

00:04:54.352 --> 00:04:59.357
OTHER, AND BOTH OF US JUST CAN'T

00:04:57.122 --> 00:05:00.058
WRAP OUR HEADS AROUND WHAT

00:04:59.491 --> 00:05:02.994
EXACTLY HAPPENED.

00:05:00.191 --> 00:05:06.598
IT DOES NOT FEEL REAL.

00:05:03.128 --> 00:05:08.066
AND SHE DOES NOT FEEL SAFE.

00:05:06.731 --> 00:05:09.601
&gt;&gt; Tucker: I BET SHE DOES NOT.

